Access rules:
1. Same class
2. Same package
3. Different package
4. Different package with inheritance


What are Access Modifiers?

Access Modifiers control the visibility (accessibility) of classes, variables, methods, and constructors.

They determine who can access what.

Imagine your house:

Bedroom  → Only You (private)

Living Room → Family (protected)

Hall → Guests (default)

Main Gate → Everyone (public)

Java uses the same idea.

Types of Access Modifiers

Java has 4 access modifiers.

Modifier	Accessible From
public	Everywhere
protected	Same package + Child classes
default (no keyword)	Same package only
private	Same class only